<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rueda de Jalón</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rueda de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalon">Jalón</a> is a village on the Jalón River west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> in Aragon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, below a ruined Islamic castle. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> took Zaragoza in 1110 the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hud">Hudid dynasty</a> held out there, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zafadola">Ahmad Sayf al-Dawla</a> (Zafadola) handed it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vii-of-leon-and-castile">Alfonso VII of Castile</a> in the 1130s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rueda-de-jalon.jpg" alt="Rueda de Jalón" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ecelan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rueda_de_Jal%C3%B3n_-_Vista_02.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
